    "q-270035": {
      "dom_id": "step-q270035",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{1-\\sqrt{3}}^{1+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}+2x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+2x+3 & =-({x}^{2}-2x)+3 \\\\  & =-(({x}^{2}-2x+1)-1)+3 \\\\  & =-((x-1)^{2}-1)+3 \\\\  & =-(x-1)^{2}+1+3 \\\\  & =4-(x-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1-\\sqrt{3}}^{1+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}+2x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1-\\sqrt{3}}^{1+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4-(x-1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1-\\sqrt{3}}^{1+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4(1-(x-1)^{2}/4)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1-\\sqrt{3}}^{1+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x-1)^{2}/{2}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{1-\\sqrt{3}}^{1+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x-1)/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x-1}{2}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x-1}{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=2\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $1-\\sqrt{3}$ | $1+\\sqrt{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1-\\sqrt{3}}^{1+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{-{x}^{2}+2x+3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{1-\\sqrt{3}}^{1+\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x-1)/2)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}/2}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot 2\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}/2}^{\\sqrt{3}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{-\\sqrt{3}/2}^{\\sqrt{3}/2} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
